  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The Hebrew and Ugaritic forms begin with y where Arabic and Sabaic have w. The Ebla list offers a possible early anatomical parallel, although the meaning of its entry is uncertain. The similar-looking names Jarmuth, Jeremoth and Jeremai share the catalogue grouping, but their consonants give no basis for deriving them from ירכ."
